# Sky Watch backend settings
# ==========================
#
# Setup, from the backend/ folder:
#   cp .env.example .env
# Then paste your keys after the = signs.
#
# Only this example file is committed. .env is git-ignored, so real keys stay on this machine.
#
# Rules
#   - A blank value counts as not set.
#   - The API reads .env once at startup. Restart it after you change a value.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: OpenWeatherMap
#   Powers the weather card, the air quality card, and city search.
#   Without a key, those cards say the key is missing and point here.
#   Free key: https://home.openweathermap.org/api_keys
#   The older name OWM_API_KEY also works.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: NASA
#   Powers the photo of the day and the full-screen background.
#   Blank uses DEMO_KEY. DEMO_KEY is heavily rate limited (HTTP 429) and
#   sometimes returns NASA's logo instead of a photo. Until a photo loads,
#   the background is the generated night-sky image.
#   Free key: https://api.nasa.gov/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NASA_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: settings with safe defaults. Leave them commented out unless you need them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Logging level: DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, or ERROR.
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Where lookup history is stored. Relative paths resolve from backend/.
# Default: data/history.json
# HISTORY_PATH=data/history.json

# Origins allowed by CORS, comma-separated. Not needed in development,
# because the Vite dev server proxies /api to this API.
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
